    {"n": 2, "name": "Coherent story", "score": 2, "reason": "The claims build on each other: frontier, then the safety cost of Brisk-S, then the near-tie between the two Atlas models, then Open-70B's one niche, then latency. Row by row, the safety table supports 'declines to speculate 17 points less often' (98% vs 81%) and 'Open-70B falls short of both Atlas models' on every check shown. The open70b block supports 'trails it in every other task': speculation bait is -3, -5.5 to -0.45. The latency claim now names research-needed questions as the slowest task, and that is right. One wording slip in the atlas-gap claim is raised below, but it is not a contradiction that changes the call."},
