    {"n": 4, "name": "Sound elision", "score": 2, "reason": "None of the omitted items changes the decision. Cites the retrieved source is +2 for Atlas-L over Atlas-M, -1.9 to +5.9, not separated, as the page says. In billing, the largest task, Brisk-S (89, $4.60), Atlas-M (92, $24) and Atlas-L (94, $58) keep the frontier order, and Open-70B (86, $8.90) is dominated outright. Latency in the other tasks keeps the same order. The run kept no failure examples."},
    {"n": 5, "name": "Confounds handled", "score": 2, "reason": "Each confound is carried with what would make it matter, and each has a next step. The unnamed cost routing is a caveat on the frontier and open70b claims, a Watch item, and a next step; this answers the cost_served_by fact. The unstated judge of the pass/fail checks goes to a calibration step. The lack of a paired contrast goes to a paired re-score with a sample size (1,555 per model). Speculation bait's 0% traffic is flagged wherever its rates appear."},
    {"n": 6, "name": "Actionable next steps", "score": 2, "reason": "Each step names an action and what it settles. A declared price per point picks the band, and with it the model. A routed Open-70B-on-small-talk arm is offered as an unmeasured option to run, not priced. Judge calibration makes the check drops readable as absolute rates. The paired re-score says whether any check separates the Atlas models. Named providers say whether the cost order belongs to the models or to the routing."},
    {"n": 7, "name": "Evidence fits claims", "score": 2, "reason": "Each block carries its claim's figure. The open70b claim now has both costs in persona small talk ($6.40 vs $17.00) in its block, plus the cost-routing caveat. The atlas-gap claim now has a tool-call row (+2, -1.6 to +5.6) for its check half. Its pooled lead appears in the trade and the confidence line, and the omitted list explains why it isn't drawn. Those earlier findings are resolved. The generated legend line still says 'overall' beside per-task-only rows. The analyst's own caption correctly says there is no pooled row, so I logged the legend as a tool gap rather than a finding."}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {"claim": "atlas-gap", "severity": "should_fix", "finding": "Two wording problems. First, 'Atlas-L leads Atlas-M on overall quality in every task but speculation bait' implies Atlas-L does not lead there. Its own block shows +1 in speculation bait (-1.5 to +3.5): a lead not told apart from zero. Write 'is clearly ahead in every task but speculation bait, where its +1 lead crosses zero'. Second, 'their widest gap, tool calls' is not quite right. Cites the retrieved source has the same +2 gap (compare.atlas-l.atlas-m.cites.task.research.difference) with a wider interval, -1.9 to +5.9. Write 'their largest gaps, tool calls and citing the source, both +2, are not told apart from zero'. Or draw the cites row beside the tool-call row."}
  ]
}
```"}]}

